From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xiaoyu Guan <xiaoyuguan@hotmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] font-set: restore the notification glyph and keep pgrep quiet

Omarchy 4.0.6 calls omarchy-notification-send with an empty -g, so the
headline is taken as the glyph and the restart reminder for Ghostty and
Foot fails with a usage message. pgrep also prints the terminals' PIDs
into the caller's terminal.

Use the glyph upstream restored in 4.5 (U+E659) and discard pgrep's
output.
---
 bin/omarchy-font-set | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bin/omarchy-font-set b/bin/omarchy-font-set
index 080f055..9c42cf1 100755
--- a/bin/omarchy-font-set
+++ b/bin/omarchy-font-set
@@ -73,12 +73,12 @@ XML
 
 omarchy-restart-shell
 
-if pgrep -x ghostty; then
-  omarchy-notification-send -g  "You must restart Ghostty to see font change"
+if pgrep -x ghostty >/dev/null; then
+  omarchy-notification-send -g  "You must restart Ghostty to see font change"
 fi
 
-if pgrep -x foot; then
-  omarchy-notification-send -g  "You must restart Foot to see font change"
+if pgrep -x foot >/dev/null; then
+  omarchy-notification-send -g  "You must restart Foot to see font change"
 fi
 
 omarchy-hook font-set "$font_name"
-- 
2.56.0

